 it a "Tier-II" city.", "newValue": "Asansol, a prominent city located in the Indian state of West Bengal, emerged as a significant urban center during the 19th century, primarily due to its strategic location along the coal-rich Damodar River basin. Established as a municipality in 1864, Asansol quickly developed into a bustling hub for trade and commerce, driven by the burgeoning coal mining industry that supported Britain's industrial ambitions. This city is pivotal in understanding the economic transformations that took place in South Asia during the colonial era, illustrating the broader implications of British imperialism on local economies and societies.

